window.docContents[6].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.Refinement/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___Refinement":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Theorems › Refinement.leanTier 1 · theorem file\n\nTier 1 · theorem file used by the symbolic proof 1 headline theorem 59 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. This file states headline theorems. Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.This file is in the non-default library CliElfLib (its theorems need the ELF built from source). Its theorems are not among the headline theorems that the closure tool lists.\n\n\n\nTrace Refinement for the libsignal-cli BinaryTrusted: the statement.Proves comp_refines_cli_placed (CompRefinesCliBinaryPlaced cliElfBytes, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean), built by lake build CliElfLib. Across every pair of multi-block placements (mpl, mmpl) linked in cliElfBytes (LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliElf.lean), the compiled AArch64 libsignal-cli binary refines the composed PQXDH ∘ SPQR ∘ Triple Ratchet symbolic model up to cryptographic byte collisions, and every reachable guarded CLI call terminates with a process outcome (CliElfProgressPlaced: no fault, trap, or divergence; SIGABRT aborts terminate the trace at CliTraces.stop).Combined with Symbolic/Theorems/ModelSecurity.lean via comp_refinement_preservation_cli (Symbolic/Theorems/RefinementPreservation.lean), this yields signal_session_secure_placed (Symbolic/Theorems/Security.lean). Non-vacuity of the extern and hook hypotheses is proved in Symbolic/Tests/ExternWitness.lean; placement witnesses and symbol-label gate A (A-LINK, Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md) are exported in Symbolic/Theorems/Security.lean.\n\n\n\ntheorem comp_refines_cli_placedL46–60 ↗#Relocatable trace refinement and progress for the SHA-256-pinned libsignal-cli AArch64 binary (CompRefinesCliBinaryPlaced cliElfBytes, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean). For every pair of multi-block placements mpl (libsignalSessionLib.LinkedAt cliElfBytes mpl) and mmpl (VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib.LinkedAt cliElfBytes mmpl), cliElfBytes parses as an ELF image satisfying CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced mpl mmpl, every reachable guarded CLI call terminates with a process outcome (CliElfProgressPlaced mpl mmpl), and under any valid cryptographic extern interpretation and matching CLI hooks, every guarded execution trace of cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl from initDirs is explained by a reachable model run (Explains) or encounters a cryptographic collision after an explained prefix (CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Theorems/Refinement.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.Refinement/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___Refinement"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.KemCorrect/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___KemCorrect":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Assumptions › KemCorrect.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 64 of 113 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nδ-correctness and cryptographic well-formedness of the PQXDH primitivesTrusted: definitions used by the statement. kemHonestExchangeFails, KemDeltaCorrect, CryptoWellFormedDh, CryptoWellFormedKemδ and CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδ are read by the δ-statement (Security/HeadlineDelta.lean under Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/); see Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Kyber-1024 (libcrux_ml_kem::kyber1024 in libsignal) has a small nonzero decapsulation-failure probability (DEV-PQ21) rather than perfect KEM correctness (WellFormedPrimitives.kem_corr). Together with WellFormedPrimitivesδ (Model.lean), this file defines KemDeltaCorrect P δ, bounding the honest failure probability by δ, and CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδ P, recording the X25519 and Kyber-1024 public-key collision bounds and wire-length rejection laws. The bound δ is taken as a hypothesis: FIPS 203 (Aug. 2024, Table 1) gives δ = 2^-174.8 for ML-KEM-1024 and the Kyber v3.02 specification (§1.4, Table 1) gives 2^-174 under heuristic noise models.\n\n\n\nδ-correctness of the KEM\n\ndef kemHonestExchangeFailsL42–48 ↗#Honest KEM decapsulation-failure event for key-generation seed seed and encapsulation coins r: encapsulation succeeds with some (ss, ct), yet decapsulation under the paired secret key does not return some ss (encapsulation returning none is not counted).\n\ndef KemDeltaCorrectL50–57 ↗#δ-correctness of the KEM (Fiedler–Günther, ePrint 2024/702, §2; FIPS 203 §3.3): kemHonestExchangeFails P seed r occurs with probability at most δ over uniform 64-byte seed and 32-byte r.\n\nCryptographic well-formedness\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedDhL61–85 ↗#Cryptographic X25519 and cofactor-8 subgroup laws on P: public-key collision bound, scalar-multiplication injectivity modulo pow8, and 32-byte length of base-point subgroup preimages.\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedKemδL87–106 ↗#Cryptographic Kyber-1024 laws on P: public-key collision bound and wire-length rejection for ciphertexts and public keys.\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδL108–111 ↗#Cryptographic well-formedness of P without perfect KEM correctness (kem_corr), combining WellFormedPrimitivesδ P, CryptoWellFormedDh P, and CryptoWellFormedKemδ P.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/KemCorrect.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.KemCorrect/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___KemCorrect"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.Statement/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___Statement":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement › Statement.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 4 headline theorems depend on it 335 of 430 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: none; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (49)structure CliCalldef CliCall.extradef FilesVisibledef InputsForstructure CliTurndef CliTurn.initdef CliTurn.recordsdef CliTurn.opkUseddef SamePathdef scrubdef BundleFilesFlatdef HonestBundleFilesdef PreKeyNoMatchdef CliTurn.afterdef CliTurn.clearSessiondef BobCallAllowedabbrev BobSetupDHSecretabbrev SetupDHSecretdef KeyInDirdef LeaksFromdef runInputdef runEventOfdef coinsLendef StdinBoundeddef FilesBoundeddef ValidCallinductive CliTracesinductive CliReachabledef dhCoinSecretsdef HonestDHSecretdef InvertsGuardeddef kyberCoinEntropydef coinDrawsdef exitedZeroDrawsdef setupDHSecretsdef CoinsFreshdef RecvBodydef ReadCollisionClidef ModelAcceptsTermAfterAttackerSendsdef RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollidedef SignalMsgAcceptedOnlyViaCollisiondef PreKeyStartCollidesOrRejectsdef PrefixExplainingGhostsdef NextEventCollidesdef CollisionAfterExplainedPrefixdef ExternContractsHoldClidef CompRefinesCliRdef CompRefinesClidef runFnToRelation\n\nWhole-Protocol Refinement Statement over signal-session CLI RunsDefines the signal-session CLI execution environment (CliCall, CliTurn, ValidCall, CliTraces, CliReachable), break/invert history guards (InvertsGuarded), CSPRNG coin-freshness premise (CoinsFresh), prefix-plus-collision excuse (CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix), and the generic trace-refinement statements (CompRefinesCliR, CompRefinesCli).\n\n\n\nstructure CliCallL41–47 ↗#Parameters of a single signal-session CLI invocation.\n\ndef CliCall.extraL49–50 ↗#\n\ndef FilesVisibleL52–58 ↗#Loader-admissibility and filesOf visibility for input file entries: excludes ., standard stream names, leading /, .. segments, and files exceeding Arm64.MAX_LFS_FILESIZE.\n\ndef InputsForL60–66 ↗#Process Inputs i corresponding to CLI call c over directory snapshot d.\n\nstructure CliTurnL68–74 ↗#Inter-call environment state: per-party directory snapshots, SignalMessage bodies emitted by earlier exit-0 send calls, and whether Bob is disabled (bobOff) after accepting an unmatched pre-key message alongside an existing session.\n\ndef CliTurn.initL76 ↗#\n\ndef CliTurn.recordsL78–82 ↗#Non-empty session record of p with its peer, if present.\n\ndef CliTurn.opkUsedL84–86 ↗#Whether Bob's one-time pre-key file has been emptied or removed.\n\ndef SamePathL88–89 ↗#Path equivalence up to Arm64.normalizePath.\n\ndef scrubL91–93 ↗#Remove coins and bundle/ entries (under any equivalent normalized path) after a run.\n\ndef BundleFilesFlatL95–97 ↗#Every bundle entry is a flat bundle/<name> path smaller than 2^31 bytes.\n\ndef HonestBundleFilesL99–102 ↗#Any bundle parsed from files by parseBundleFiles satisfies HonestBundle.\n\ndef PreKeyNoMatchL104–108 ↗#Bob recv of a non-whisper message while holding an existing session that is not eligible for promotion (¬ EligibleForSessionPromotion).\n\ndef CliTurn.afterL110–118 ↗#Updated CliTurn after call c exits with code, out, and files.\n\ndef CliTurn.clearSessionL120–126 ↗#Delete p's session file (re-enabling Bob when p = r.bob).\n\ndef BobCallAllowedL128–129 ↗#\n\nabbrev BobSetupDHSecretL131–132 ↗#\n\nabbrev SetupDHSecretL134–135 ↗#\n\ndef KeyInDirL137–142 ↗#Secrets currently present in p's directory at turn t (long-term/prekey files and keys in p's active session record).\n\ndef LeaksFromL144–145 ↗#\n\ndef runInputL147–150 ↗#\n\ndef runEventOfL152–153 ↗#\n\ndef coinsLenL155–160 ↗#Expected coins byte length for each CLI subcommand (192 for init, 64 for send, 32 for recv).\n\ndef StdinBoundedL162–174 ↗#Size bounds on c.stdin matching the binary specifications' input domains.\n\ndef FilesBoundedL176–177 ↗#\n\ndef ValidCallL179–198 ↗#Preconditions for a guarded CLI call c at turn t: coin and file bounds, BobCallAllowed, role/session state discipline, HonestBundleFiles on init, send-counter bound < 2^32 - 1 on send, and PqFromHonest on recv.\n\ninductive CliTracesL200–222 ↗#Guarded CLI event traces generated by Rel from turn t: session deletions (clear), primitive break/invert events (breakInvert), exited CLI calls preceded by directory leaks (step), and aborted CLI calls terminating the trace (stop).\n\ninductive CliReachableL224–235 ↗#Inter-call turns reachable from t₀ via exited guarded calls and session deletions.\n\ndef dhCoinSecretsL237–243 ↗#32-byte X25519 private-key slices read from ev.coins (0..32 and 160..192 for init; 0..32 for recv; none for send).\n\ndef HonestDHSecretL245–248 ↗#Whether sk is a setup X25519 secret or a dhCoinSecrets slice of an exit-0 run in evs.\n\ndef InvertsGuardedL250–259 ↗#History guard on invertDH and invertKEM events: each follows its corresponding breakDH / breakKEM event and inverts an honest setup or coin-drawn public key.\n\ndef kyberCoinEntropyL261–264 ↗#32-byte Kyber encapsulation entropy extracted from the first byte of each 4-byte CSPRNG fill at offsets 32 + 4 * j (j < 32) of an init call's coins.\n\ndef coinDrawsL266–272 ↗#Clamped 32-byte secret draws consumed by ev (dhCoinSecrets plus kyberCoinEntropy on init; dhCoinSecrets on recv; none on send).\n\ndef exitedZeroDrawsL274–277 ↗#\n\ndef setupDHSecretsL279–282 ↗#Clamped setup X25519 secrets of r (ikA, ikB, spkB, and opkB when r.withOpk holds).\n\ndef CoinsFreshL284–290 ↗#CSPRNG coin-freshness premise for security theorems: all clamped setup X25519 secrets and clamped secret coin draws of exit-0 runs in evs are pairwise distinct (List.Nodup). Refinement theorems (CompRefinesCli*) do not assume CoinsFresh.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 292–294): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesDY.Libsignal.Composed.Refinement.Cli.instDecidableCoinsFresh\n\ndef RecvBodyL296–301 ↗#Inner SignalMessage body b of a received whisper or pre-key wire frame input.\n\ndef ReadCollisionCliL303–313 ↗#Whether ss already read a colliding network term on an earlier exit-0 recv event in evs.\n\ndef ModelAcceptsTermAfterAttackerSendsL315–324 ↗#Whether extending (g, ss) by attacker-known network steps and one decrypt step reading t explains evs₁ ++ [.run ev].\n\ndef RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollideL326–339 ↗#Under explanation (g', ss', vis') of evs₁, either every representation of b hits RecvCollisionOn ∨ ReselectCollisionOn, or at least one representation is accepted for ev and every accepted representation hits RecvCollisionOn.\n\ndef SignalMsgAcceptedOnlyViaCollisionL341–349 ↗#SignalMessage body b in ev has a symbolic representation under (g, ss) and hits RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollide under every collision-free explanation of evs₁.\n\ndef PreKeyStartCollidesOrRejectsL351–360 ↗#Pre-key message p (wire bytes b) starts a Bob session only via KyberMismatch or BobSessionStartCollidesOrImplicitRejectsOn across all collision-free explanations of evs₁.\n\ndef PrefixExplainingGhostsL362–365 ↗#Ghosts sharing g.σ that explain evs₁ via the same step sequence ss.\n\ndef NextEventCollidesL367–391 ↗#Next run event ev after explained prefix evs₁ forces a cryptographic collision on either an exit-0 recv or the plaintext of a send.\n\ndef CollisionAfterExplainedPrefixL393–401 ↗#Some prefix evs₁ of evs is explained by (g, ss, vis), and the immediately following run event forces NextEventCollides.\n\ndef ExternContractsHoldCliL403–407 ↗#Machine-independent external crypto contracts: ExternCryptoLawsHold, canonical X25519 public keys, and rejection of X25519 torsion shifts.\n\ndef CompRefinesCliRL409–421 ↗#Whole-protocol CLI trace refinement starting from initial directory family dirs: for every valid interp, agreeing W, and well-formed r, there exist opaque semantics S such that every guarded trace evs is either explained (Explains) or hits CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix.\n\ndef CompRefinesCliL423–426 ↗#Whole-protocol CLI trace refinement starting from initDirs.\n\ndef runFnToRelationL428–431 ↗#\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/Statement.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.Statement/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___Statement"}});